 "text": "Hi, how you doing right now? Generally, a few weeks are enough. The oil sets deeply at first, so it' worth waiting for it to dry completely. Six months is way too early, oil painting takes years to fully mature. If you want to see significant progress, you could varnish it with a water based varnish after a few weeks. Then re varnish with oil based varnish in a few years. Touch dry in few weeks, feels dry to the touch. Fully dry in few months, can be worn while it waits.",
